course: dictionary
lesson: 14107
title: Formal words that praise
level: primary-4
stars: 0
explain: Some words sound grown-up because they belong to formal places, like the army, the police and award ceremonies. You can still work them out from the words around them. «The officer received a medal for meritorious bravery.» Medals are given for something special, so meritorious must be about deserving praise.
explain: Look inside the word for clues. Merit means a good quality that earns praise, and -ious means full of. So meritorious means full of merit. Then test your meaning in the sentence: "deserving praise" should still make sense.
explain: Look for the feeling in the sentence. «Her meritorious work on the class garden earned a certificate.» Certificates are given for good work, so the author is praising her. Formal words often tell you that someone has done something very good.
fact: Meritorious means deserving praise or reward because it is very good or brave.
fact: «Meritorious» is a formal word, so you will mostly meet it in serious writing and official settings.
fact: «Meritorious Service Medal» is the name of an award, used in the army and police.
fact: In school, merit badges and certificates reward meritorious work or behaviour.
fact: Phrases you may see are «meritorious service» and «meritorious conduct».
exercise: «The firefighter received a medal for her meritorious bravery.» What does meritorious mean? | Quick and noisy | Left over from before | Very wet and muddy | *Deserving praise for being very good or brave
exercise: Ben says meritorious is just another word for messy. What does it really mean? | Hidden under the ground | Messy and untidy | Very tired after a long day | *Deserving praise or reward
exercise: Find the word in «The school gave Maya a certificate for meritorious work» that shows she is being rewarded. | gave | Maya | school | *certificate
test: Which word is closest in meaning to meritorious? | Rude | Hidden | *Praiseworthy | Lazy
test: Which action would most likely earn a Meritorious Service Medal? | Arriving late for school | *Showing brave and very good service for the army | Losing a game on purpose | Forgetting your homework
exam: Which sentence uses meritorious correctly? | *The soldier's meritorious service earned her a medal | The cat was meritorious and slept on the sofa all day | The rain was meritorious and fell for hours | I felt meritorious about the long queue for lunch
